    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27115" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luctĭfĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>causing sorrow</i> or <i>lamentation, doleful,
				woful, baleful</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clades, Cic. poët. Tusc. 2, 10, 25:
					Alecto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 324</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 557</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jubar,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 292</span></i>
			.—<i>Neutr.</i> as adv.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luctificum clangente tuba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 348</span></i>
			.</div>
